#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0311 expect=violation domain=CO
#note "Rows 1 and 2 share the key tuple (COSEQ, USUBJID) = (1, 001) and GroupSemantics.uniqueSetViolations flags the first-seen row AND the repeat, so the count is 2. Rows 3 and 4 are unique tuples. Rows 5 and 6 are the DISCRIMINATOR: under FOLD_BLANK_KEYS a blank USUBJID is a real key component so they ARE a duplicate tuple and the operator flags them, but the leading `not empty(USUBJID)` conjunct -- the sheet's own Condition cell 'USUBJID ^= null' -- masks them out of the violation set. Count 2, not 4, is the assertion. M3-D20 added Output_Variables [USUBJID, COSEQ] (the rule previously declared none at all, one of only six rules in the family that omitted the field); no pin depends on it, since #expectViolationAt falls back to the primary table's column at the fired row."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 2
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=001 COSEQ=1
#expectViolationAt row=2 USUBJID=001 COSEQ=1
dataset CO
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col COSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col COVAL   type=Char label="Comment"
---
S1 | CO | 001 | 1 | First
S1 | CO | 001 | 1 | Duplicate
S1 | CO | 001 | 2 | Second
S1 | CO | 002 | 1 | Other subject
S1 | CO |     | 9 | Unattributed
S1 | CO |     | 9 | Unattributed again
---
